1. THE REQUIREMENT AND THE TEMPERATURE
   REQ-016 (v2/ecad/tools/pcb_requirements.yaml), verbatim: "The solar input charges the pack through board E's LT8705A stage from a panel inside its declared window: an open-circuit voltage of at most 25 V at the panel's coldest operating temperature, the panel held at 17.6 V by the stage's input regulation, and at most 100 W into the stage."
   read: at most 25 V open circuit at the panel's coldest operating temperature; held at 17.6 V; at most 100 W into the stage;
   its acceptance: F2 and J_SOLAR rated 10 A. A series diode or a clamp in place of the panel's own open circuit: NOT admitted (the statement constrains the panel's own open circuit; D4 is judged apart under TRN-001)
   the coldest operating temperature: -20 C, REQ-024's in-use minimum (-20 to +40 C ambient; pcb_envelope.yaml in_use agrees);
   the records settle REQ-016's reading at the kit's use boundary (L4-ENERGY-ARCHITECTURE.md, 'What stays INCONCLUSIVE'); the
   panels' own -40 C ratings are printed for information only.
   SESSION (the assumption the brief asks to state): with no irradiance the cells sit at the ambient; the bound puts STC
   irradiance (1000 W/m2) on cells still at -20 C, a cold clear sunrise before the cells warm. Less irradiance only lowers Voc;
   an edge-of-cloud 1250 W/m2 is printed beside it as a sensitivity (the fit's log term, INFERRED), not as part of the bound.
   owner rulings in the registry naming a panel class (a class word beside 'panel' or 'array' in one sentence): none; a1solar SELECTION.md 1 (a session's criterion) prefers folding, semi-rigid or blanket for a carried kit

