7. THE WINDOW AGAINST THE PRINTED BANDS (the gap, INFERRED on the model)
   A band's spread is its top over its bottom (as factors on the rated Voc). A panel of a given curve shape is bounded at 25 V
   only while its band top is at most k_bound (25 V over its rated Voc at -20 C) and is held only while its band bottom is at least
   k_reach (the hold's upper corner over its rated Voc at noon; the fit's Voc scales exactly with the voltages, checked). Both
   hold for some rating only while the spread is at most W = k_bound / k_reach.
   SunPower SPR-E-Flex-100                                      k_bound 1.0395; k_reach 0.9383 (18.813 V) / 0.9087 (18.221 V); W 1.1079 / 1.1439 (symmetric +-5.12 / +-6.71 %); printed spread 1.2222: WIDER than W, no rating of this shape and band fits both
   BougeRV 100W N-Type Fiberglass Foldable (SP001-BK-GRUSGA)    k_bound 1.1238; k_reach 1.0213 (18.813 V) / 0.9891 (18.221 V); W 1.1003 / 1.1361 (symmetric +-4.78 / +-6.37 %); printed spread 1.1579: WIDER than W, no rating of this shape and band fits both
   Solbian SX 156                                               k_bound 1.0260; k_reach 0.9434 (18.813 V) / 0.9137 (18.221 V); W 1.0875 / 1.1229 (symmetric +-4.19 / +-5.79 %); printed spread none printed
   For the rated rows as they stand, the band a maker would have to print: SunPower +3.95 / -6.17 %, Solbian SX 156 +2.60 / -5.66 %
   (the top from the bound, the bottom from the conditioned upper corner's reach; the coefficient relative).
   BougeRV's rated row sits under its own reach floor (k_reach 1.0213 > 1): its rating, not only its band, is too low for the
   hold's upper corner.

