10. THE DECISION ON U-03 (SESSION, by the predicate: bounded at or under 25 V by the maker's printed band AND the hold inside
    the curve at the conditioned upper corner over that band; portable)
   SunPower SPR-E-Flex-100                                      bounded NO; hold NO; portable yes -> does not qualify
   BougeRV 100W N-Type Fiberglass Foldable (SP001-BK-GRUSGA)    bounded yes; hold NO; portable yes -> does not qualify
   Solbian SX 156                                               bounded NO; hold yes; portable yes -> does not qualify
   on EA3's typical band (upper corner 18.221 V) instead of the conditioned one: SPR does not qualify; BGV does not qualify; SBX does not qualify
   NO CANDIDATE QUALIFIES. U-03 stays an unresolved choice; it decides the solar source, not the topology (REQ-016's window,
   the stage and its hold stay). REQ-016 need not change, so no owner question is raised.
   The exact gap: no maker's document read prints an open-circuit band narrow enough for this window. SunPower's band (10 %
   of measured) reaches 26.723 V at -20 C; BougeRV's (-5 / +10 %) is bounded at 24.471 V but its curve sits under the hold
   (its rated Voc at noon 18.420 V against the conditioned upper corner 18.813 V); Solbian prints none. The window admits a spread
   of at most 1.0875 to 1.1079 (the shapes above), a symmetric band of about +-4.2 to +-5.1 %; the rated rows of the two panels
   that match the hold need a band top of at most +3.95 % (SunPower) and +2.60 % (Solbian).
   The next bounded action: (1) the makers' written open-circuit band for the two hold-matched panels, asked by the drafts in
   clarification/ (the owner sends them; the session contacts no outside party); (2) failing a written band, O-1's own
   alternative closure, a controlled unit at Layer 6: the unit bought (the owner's money) is accepted only when its Voc,
   measured at a known cell temperature and irradiance and corrected to STC with its expanded uncertainty U, lies inside
     SunPower SPR-E-Flex-100      20.079 V + U to 22.245 V - U (its coefficient's own uncertainty inside U)
     Solbian SX 156               20.094 V + U to 21.853 V - U (its coefficient's own uncertainty inside U)
   (the floor is the hold's necessary condition: a unit there gives the stage nothing at the conditioned upper corner at noon;
   the unit's own trace, rerun, decides its energy)
   A series diode or a clamp is not a substitute (section 1).
   THE DOWNSTREAM ITEM (Layer 6, component selection; the purchase is the owner's): PANEL-ACC. Accept the bought panel when
   the maker's document of the bought revision, filed with its sha256, bounds Voc at -20 C at or under 25 V by section 3's rule
   and its band keeps the hold inside the curve by section 4's rule, or, failing a printed band, when the unit itself passes the
   window above; then rerun its trace through the replay's section 12 and L4-E7's section 5 (A1 and A2), and re-read the
   entry's 10 A for its hot short circuit.

11. EVIDENCE CLASSES: MAKER (SunPower's sheet and guide, Solbian's sheet), MAKER-PAGE (BougeRV's page, transcribed), RECORD
    (the replay's and L4-E7's outputs), MODELED (the energy record's single-diode model and day), INFERRED (the window ratios,
    the cell temperature at the hot end, the edge-of-cloud term), ASSUMPTION (a band's voltages scaled with its currents kept;
    BougeRV's rows taken as STC), SESSION (the temperature reading, the 10 % sentence's reading, the coefficient as a fraction,
    the hold predicate and the day's 5 % hours, the conditioned band as the judged band).
